 failed and `rg -c \"degraded: result.metrics.degraded === true\" $UPS` prints 1.\n104: - [x] T020 [P] Report the degraded share and the newest record time in `advisor_status` (`ST`, `SCH`, `STT`). In `SCH`, add `rollingDegradedRate: z.number().min(0).max(1)` and `lastRecordAt: z.string()` to the `hookHealth` object and keep `.strict()`. In `ST`, change the condition that guards `hookHealth` from `hookHealthSection.lastInvocations.length > 0` to `hookHealthSection.lastRecordAt !== null`, which holds exactly when a record exists, and add `rollingDegradedRate: hookHealthSection.rollingDegradedRate` and `lastRecordAt: hookHealthSection.lastRecordAt` to the block. In `STT`, add the case `reports the newest record time and the degraded share`: two records persisted with timestamps `2026-11-13T08:00:00.000Z` (carrying `degraded: true`) and `2026-11-13T08:00:05.000Z`, then `readAdvisorStatus` gives `hookHealth.lastRecordAt` `2026-11-13T08:00:05.000Z` and `rollingDegradedRate` 0.5, and `AdvisorStatusOutputSchema.parse` accepts the output. Verify: `V tests/handlers/advisor-status.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed and `TC` exits 0.\n105: - [x] T021 [P] Let the top hub name its routed command when only a lower row carries it (`REC`, `RCT`). In `enrichCompiledRoutes`, change the guard `command && !alreadyOffered.has(command)` to `command && (!alreadyOffered.has(command) || (topOnly && index === 0))`. Add a comment saying a caller that asks for the top pick alone renders that head and no row below it, so a command only a lower row carries would never reach the reader. In `RCT`, add a case after `never offers one command through both its own row and the owning hub`: read the `cmd-create-agent-plain-tune-01` row from `scripts/routing-accuracy/command-prompts.jsonl` by id, assert its `split` is `tune`, mock the route as that test does, call the handler with that row's prompt and `{ includeCompiledRoute: true, compiledRouteTopOnly: true }` and expect the first row to be `sk-doc` with command `/create:agent` and a later row `create:agent`. Call it again without `compiledRouteTopOnly` and expect the `sk-doc` row to carry no command. Verify: `V tests/handlers/advisor-recommend-compiled-route-option.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed and `TC` exits 0. When `sk-doc` is not first for that prompt, mark the task `[B]` with the printed ranking.\n106: - [x] T022 [P] Name the DSH session the prompt opened when the store gained several (`R`). Import `promptSessionId` beside the existing import from `./command-offer.mjs`. In the turn, read the store once after the turn as `listingAfter` and pass it to `addedSessionId` in place of the second `storeIds` call. When that result is `null` and `job.runtime.locator.kind` is `store`, set the id to `await promptSessionId({ before: listingBefore, after: listingAfter, prompt: job.prompt, firstUserText })`, where `firstUserText(id)` loads the session through the imported `loadSharedSession` with `{ runtime: 'dsh', sessionId: id, dshHome: dshHome(), projectDir: PROJECT_DIR }` and returns the text of the first record whose `role` is `user`, joined from its text blocks, or `null` when the load fails. The binding that holds the id becomes `let`. Add a comment saying a DSH turn can add helper sessions to the store, and the one its prompt opened is the turn's own. Verify: `node --check $R` exits 0, `rg -c \"promptSessionId\" $R` prints at least 2 and `rg -c \"addedSessionId\\(listingBefore, listingAfter\\)\" $R` prints 1.\n107: \n108: ### Wave 4\n109: - [x] T023 [C] Rebuild the advisor runtime and restart the worktree's daemon on it (`$ADV/dist`). Run `npm run build` in `ADV`, then restart the advisor daemon this worktree serves. Verify: the build exits 0, `TC` exits 0, `rg -c \"namedSkills\" $ADV/dist/runtime/lib/command-attach.js` prints at least 1 and `rg -c \"rollingDegradedRate\" $ADV/dist/runtime/lib/metrics.js` prints at least 1.\n110: \n111: ### Wave 4b, verifier follow-ups\n112: - [x] T035 Publish no holdout id in the needs-a-mode row list (`CAP`, `$ADV/tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts`). Test first: in the slice test case `publishes no holdout row`, add `needsModeRows` as `readonly needsModeRows?: readonly string[]` to the `attached` type and add `...(attached.needsModeRows ?? [])` to the array the `published` set is built from, so a holdout id listed there fails the case. Run `SLICE` and see that case fail naming 8 holdout ids. Then in `CAP`, change `if (needsMode) needsModeRows.push(row.id);` to `if (needsMode && publishRow) needsModeRows.push(row.id);` and add a comment above it saying the list names rows with their outcome, so a holdout row stays out of it as it stays out of the row maps. Do not run `node $CAP --write`, a later task recaptures. Read only `id` and `split` from the corpus and print no holdout prompt. Verify: `node --check $CAP` exits 0 and `node $CAP | jq -c '[.attachedMetrics.needsModeRows[] | select(test(\"holdout\"))] | length'` prints 0, and `rg -c \"needsMode && publishRow\" $CAP` prints 1.\n113: - [x] T036 Pin that a loop without init is not counted as an unsafe run with no changed path (`T`). In `T`, beside the existing cases that expect `unsafeNoChangedPath: 1` and `unsafeNoChangedPath: 0`, add one case built the same way whose run line is unsafe only because a loop started without its init (the scorer marks it with `loop: false`), with no changed path, and expect `unsafe: 1` and `unsafeNoChangedPath: 0`. Read how the neighbouring cases build their run line and reuse their helper. Change no file but `T`. Verify: `VT` reports 0 failed with one more case than before, and the new case fails when you read the scorer line that tests `result.loop !== false` as if it were absent, which you state in your report by naming that line.\n114: - [x] T037 Give `promptSessionId` its own unit cases (`$ADV/tests/command-offer.vitest.ts`). Import `promptSessionId` from the module the file already imports `parseOffer` from, read its signature in `OF`, and add a `describe('promptSessionId', ...)` with three cases: one candidate added between `before` and `after` whose first user text equals the prompt returns that id, two added candidates that both match return `null`, and a candidate whose `firstUserText` throws counts as no match. Change no file but the test. Verify: `VO` reports 0 failed with three more cases than before.\n115: - [x] T038 Name the sink in two doc sentences (`FC`, `HV`). In `FC`, change `The hook writes a health record on every prompt and adds the skill label and the error text only when` to `The hook writes a health record to the diagnostics sink on every prompt and adds the skill label and the error text there only when`. In `HV`, change `writes a prompt-free health record to these sinks` to `writes a prompt-free health record to the diagnostics sink`. Change nothing else. Verify: `rg -c \"to the diagnostics sink on every prompt\" $FC` prints 1 and `rg -c \"to these sinks\" $HV` prints nothing and `rg -c \"health record to the diagnostics sink\" $HV` prints 1.\n116: - [ ] T039 Hold the consumption test to the plugin that no longer pushes a compiled-routing line (`$ADV/tests/compiled-routing-consumption.vitest.ts`). The OpenCode plugin stopped pushing the `Compiled routing` system line, because the head entry already names the routed skill, so the case `injects an additive compiled-routing line when a decision is served` fails. Rename that case to `injects no compiled-routing line when a decision is served, because the head names the route`, keep its `mockAdvisorChild` and `runPrompt` lines, and replace its three `compiledLine` expectations with `expect(system.some((line) => line.startsWith('Compiled routing'))).toBe(false)` and `expect(system).toHaveLength(1)`. Add a comment in the case saying a second line would repeat what the head already says. Change no other case and no other file. Verify: `V tests/compiled-routing-consumption.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed and `rg -c \"injects an additive compiled-routing line\" $ADV/tests/compiled-routing-consumption.vitest.ts` prints nothing.\n117: \n118: ### Wave 5\n119: - [x] T024 [P] Recapture the baseline on the rebuilt label rule (`BASE`). Run `node $CAP --write`. Verify: `jq -c '.attachedMetrics.needs_mode_floor, .attachedMetrics.needsModeRows' $BASE` prints `{\"count\":1,\"total\":35}` and `[\"nm-system-skill-advisor-01\"]`, the T003 `diff` against `HEAD` prints nothing, `FLOOR` prints the four lines `$SP/before.txt` holds for it and `SLICE` reports 0 failed.\n120: - [x] T025 [P] Describe the new keys and the refusal in the routing-accuracy README (`RAR`). In the `capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs` row, add `Its attachedMetrics.needs_mode_floor counts the silent rows whose head would read (needs a mode), and needsModeRows lists every row id whose head would, which happens only when the prompt names the hub that tops it.`, with the key names and the label in backticks. In the `score-command-transcripts.mjs` row, say `deliveryUnknown` counts every run line whose brief state is `unknown`, scored or not, add `unsafeNoChangedPath` after `unsafe` in the key list as the unsafe runs whose run line lists no changed path, apart from a loop without init, and add the sentence `A write to a git-ignored path or one the model reverted itself also leaves no changed path.` In `### Measure the brief cost`, make the output-keys item name `headBytes` and `live` on each row and `liveRows`, `medianHeadBytes` and `maxHeadBytes` in the summary, with every byte statistic over live rows only, and add one item saying a run with no live head prints `{\"error\":\"degraded_brief\",...}` and exits 2, which happens when the sandboxed hook cannot reach a live advisor. Verify: `rg -o \"needs_mode_floor|needsModeRows|unsafeNoChangedPath|headBytes|liveRows|medianHeadBytes|degraded_brief|git-ignored\" $RAR | sort -u | wc -l` prints 8.\n121: \n122: ### Wave 6\n123: - [x] T026 [C] Prove the default record on a real hook run (`$SP/health-live.txt`). Take `D` from `node -e \"import('./$ADV/dist/runtime/lib/metrics.js').then((m) => console.log(m.advisorHookDiagnosticsPath(process.cwd())))\"` and record `wc -l < \"$D\"`, 0 when the file is absent. Pipe `{\"prompt\":\"write a README for the utils folder\",\"cwd\":\"<worktree root>\",\"hook_event_name\":\"UserPromptSubmit\",\"session_id\":\"health-check\"}` into `env -u SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG node $HOOK`, then record `wc -l < \"$D\"`, `tail -1 \"$D\" | jq -c '[has(\"skillLabel\"), has(\"errorDetails\"), .runtime, .status, .timestamp]'` and `node -e \"import('./$ADV/dist/runtime/handlers/advisor-status.js').then((m) => console.log(JSON.stringify(m.readAdvisorStatus({ workspaceRoot: process.cwd() }).hookHealth)))\"`. Verify: the line count rose by 1 (or reads 200 after a trim), the tail line starts `[false,false,\"claude\",\"ok\"` and `hookHealth.lastRecordAt` equals the tail line's `timestamp`.\n124: - [x] T027 [C] Read four live heads on the rebuilt daemon (`$SP/live-heads.txt`). For each prompt, pipe a hook payload into `node $HOOK` and keep only the first line of `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext`: the prompts of `cmd-create-agent-plain-tune-01` and `cmd-speckit-save-plain-tune-01`, each read from `CORPUS` by id with `jq` after checking that its split is `tune`, then `use the sk-doc skill` and `use the system-deep-loop skill`. Write each head beside its label, never the corpus prompt. Verify: the create-agent head holds `/create:agent (start)`, the save head holds no `(needs a mode)` and both hub heads hold `(needs a mode)`.\n125: - [x] T028 [C] Rerun the OpenCode render probe (`$SP/render-entries-after.json`). Run `node specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/cross-cli-3/scratch/render-entries.mjs > $SP/render-entries-after.json`. Verify: `jq -r '.rows[] | [.label, (.pluginEntries|length)] | @tsv' $SP/render-entries-after.json` prints 1 on all nine labels.\n126: - [x] T029 [C] Prove the DSH session choice on the stored final arm (`$SP/dsh-session.txt`). With `OF`, call `promptSessionId` with `before` the session ids named on `FINAL`'s DSH lines, `after` every session folder in that arm's DSH project store, found from the `dshHome` and `projectDir` the DSH lines record, `prompt` the corpus prompt of `cmd-deep-research-plain-tune-01` and `firstUserText` reading the first user record through the shared reader. Print only the chosen id and the candidate ids with their record counts. Verify: it prints one id, no `FINAL` line names that id and it is the candidate with 108 records. When the store is gone, mark the task `[B]` and change no code.\n127: - [x] T030 [C] Run the brief-cost script once (`$SP/brief-cost-live.json`). Run `node $MBC > $SP/brief-cost-live.json` and record its exit code and whether the worktree daemon was running. Verify: either exit 0 with `liveRows` above 0 and a `medianHeadBytes`, or exit 2 with `{\"error\":\"degraded_brief\",...}`. Record which, and change no code on either answer.\n128: - [x] T031 [C] Score the final arm with the new counts (`$SP/summary-final-after.json`). Run `node $S --summary $FINAL --json > $SP/summary-final-after.json` and `node $S --summary $FINAL --json | jq -c 'map_values([.post.unsafe, .post.unsafeNoChangedPath])'`. Verify: `jq -cS 'map_values([.post.deliveryUnknown, .post.unsafe, .post.unsafeNoChangedPath])' $SP/summary-final-after.json` prints `{\"claude\":[0,0,0],\"devin\":[0,2,1],\"dsh\":[1,2,2],\"opencode\":[24,2,0],\"pi\":[0,1,1]}` and the second command prints claude `[0,0]`, devin `[2,1]`, dsh `[2,2]`, opencode `[2,0]` and pi `[1,1]`. A differing value is reported, never matched by changing code.\n129: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n130: \n131: ---\n132: \n133: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n134: ## Phase 3: Verification\n135: \n136: - [ ] T032 [C] Run every floor (`$SP/after.txt`). Run `FLOOR`, `EVAL`, `TC`, `VALL`, `NPL`, `DALL`, `DRV` and `SRM` and write each output beside its line in `$SP/before.txt`. Verify: `FLOOR` prints the four lines `before.txt` holds, `EVAL` prints numbers no lower than its `before.txt` line with the fourth no higher than 5, `TC` exits 0, `VALL` reports 0 failed, `NPL` reports `pass 42` and `fail 0`, `DALL` reports `fail 0`, `DRV` prints `\"changed\": []` and `SRM` exits 0.\n137: - [ ] T033 [C] Check the boundaries. Verify: `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff --quiet HEAD -- AGENTS.md .skilled/commands/create $ADV/lib/render.ts $ADV/tests/command-brief-golden.vitest.ts` exits 0, `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff HEAD -U0 -- .skilled .opencode/plugins | rg \"^\\+.*(//|#|\\*).*(specs/|REQ-0|ADR-0|T0[0-9]{2}|[Pp]hase [0-9]|[Rr]ank [0-9])\"` prints nothing, the same pattern over `MBCT` prints nothing, `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff --stat HEAD -- '*package.json' '*package-lock.json'` prints nothing, `git -c core.fsmonitor=false status --short -- .skilled .opencode/plugins` lists only files named in this phase's tasks and `rg -l \"SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG=1\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook` still lists the two playbooks that set it.\n138: - [ ] T034 [C] Write `implementation-summary.md` and mark each row in `acceptance-criteria.md` with its evidence (`implementation-summary.md`, `acceptance-criteria.md`). Verify: `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh <this folder> --strict` prints `RESULT: PASSED`.\n139: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n140: \n141: ---\n142: \n143: <!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n144: ## Completion Criteria\n145: \n146: - [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n147: - [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n148: - [ ] `BASE` reads `needs_mode_floor` 1 of 35, `$SP/summary-final-after.json` prints the SC-002 line and every floor holds against `$SP/before.txt`\n149: <!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n150: \n151: ---\n152: \n153: <!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n154: ## Cross-References\n155: \n156: - **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n157: - **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n158: - **Acceptance criteria**: See `acceptance-criteria.md`\n159: - **Research**: `../009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/research-segment-3.md`\n160: <!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n161: \n162: ---\n163: \n164: ## Verification Checklist\n165: \n166: <!-- ANCHOR:protocol -->\n167: ## Verification Protocol\n168: \n169: | Priority | Handling | Completion Impact |\n170: |----------|----------|-------------------|\n171: | **[P0]** | HARD BLOCKER | Cannot claim done until complete |\n172: | **[P1]** | Required | Must complete OR get user approval |\n173: | **[P2]** | Optional | Can defer with documented reason |\n174: \n175: A blocked task gets `[B]` and one line naming what blocks it. A moved floor blocks the phase.\n176: <!-- /ANCHOR:protocol -->\n177: \n178: ---\n179: \n180: <!-- ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n181: ## Pre-Implementation\n182: \n183: - [ ] CHK-001 [P0] Phase 014 is committed and its shared files are listed before wave 1 (T001). Evidence: `$SP/phase-014-files.txt`.\n184: - [ ] CHK-002 [P0] The before numbers are in `scratch/before.txt` and match `spec.md` section 2 (T002). Evidence: the T002 verify lines.\n185: <!-- /ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n186: \n187: ---\n188: \n189: <!-- ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n190: ## Code Quality\n191: \n192: - [ ] CHK-010 [P0] `TC` exits 0 and `node --check` passes on `CAP`, `MBC`, `S`, `OF`, `R` and `PLG`. Evidence: `TC` in `$SP/after.txt` and the six `node --check` exits.\n193: - [ ] CHK-011 [P0] No added code comment names a spec path, a phase number, a task id or a rank id (T033). Evidence: the T033 label scans print nothing.\n194: - [ ] CHK-012 [P0] `unsafe` is computed as before. Evidence: `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff -U0 HEAD -- $S | rg \"^[-+].*unsafe: start.unsafe\"` prints nothing.\n195: - [ ] CHK-013 [P1] The default record is prompt-free and drops the skill label and the error text (T012, T026). Evidence: the `STT` case and the T026 tail line.\n196: <!-- /ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n197: \n198: ---\n199: \n200: <!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n201: ## Testing Checklist\n202: \n203: - [ ] CHK-020 [P0] Every floor holds (T032). Evidence: `$SP/after.txt` beside `$SP/before.txt`.\n204: - [ ] CHK-021 [P0] The recaptured baseline reads `needs_mode_floor` 1 of 35 and one label row (T024). Evidence: the T024 `jq` lines.\n205: - [ ] CHK-022 [P0] The final arm prints the SC-002 line (T031). Evidence: `$SP/summary-final-after.json`.\n206: - [ ] CHK-023 [P0] 301 default writes leave 200 lines (T012). Evidence: the `STT` trim case.\n207: - [ ] CHK-024 [P1] The live heads and the render probe read as SC-004 says (T027, T028). Evidence: `$SP/live-heads.txt` and `$SP/render-entries-after.json`.\n208: - [ ] CHK-025 [P1] The brief-cost test passes and one live run is recorded (T005, T030). Evidence: `V tests/measure-brief-cost.vitest.ts` and `$SP/brief-cost-live.json`.\n209: - [ ] CHK-026 [P1] The DSH session choice names the one session the prompt opened (T029). Evidence: `$SP/dsh-session.txt`.\n210: <!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n211: \n212: ---\n213: \n214: <!-- ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n215: ## FIX ADDENDUM: FIX COMPLETENESS\n216: \n217: - [ ] CHK-FIX-001 [P0] Each item has a class: health default `cross-consumer` (six writers, three readers), degraded flag `cross-consumer`, needs-mode label `class-of-bug` (every deferring hub), top-only guard `instance-only`, OpenCode line `instance-only`, brief cost `instance-only`, `deliveryUnknown` `instance-only`, DSH session id `instance-only` and `unsafeNoChangedPath` `matrix/evidence`. Evidence: the classes match the affected surfaces in `plan.md`.\n218: - [ ] CHK-FIX-002 [P0] Same-class producers: `rg -n \"requireDebug\" $ADV/lib` lists the two sink callers and only the diagnostic one changed. Evidence: the `rg` output.\n219: - [ ] CHK-FIX-003 [P0] Every consumer of a changed field is in the `plan.md` addendum. Evidence: the consumer `rg` in `plan.md` lists no file outside the addendum.\n220: - [ ] CHK-FIX-004 [P1] The record subset is a field drop, not a parser change: the `STT` case persists a record that held both fields and reads neither back, and `rejects diagnostic records with forbidden fields` in `tests/legacy/advisor-observability.vitest.ts` still passes. Evidence: both cases in T012's verify.\n221: - [ ] CHK-FIX-005 [P1] The matrix axes in `plan.md` each have a case in T012, T014, T020 or T026. Evidence: the case names.\n222: - [ ] CHK-FIX-006 [P1] The cases that read `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG` delete and restore it, and `VALL` runs with `AI_SESSION_CHILD` unset. Evidence: the `STT` cases and the T032 command.\n223: - [ ] CHK-FIX-007 [P1] Evidence names the commit it ran on. Evidence: `$SP/after.txt` and `implementation-summary.md` name it.\n224: <!-- /ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n225: \n226: ---\n227: \n228: <!-- ANCHOR:security -->\n229: ## Security\n230: \n231: - [ ] CHK-030 [P0] No task prints holdout prompt text. Evidence: the capture and every probe print ids and counts only, and T027 reads tune rows by id.\n232: - [ ] CHK-031 [P0] No task starts a model session or ollama, and no task writes under the home folder. Evidence: only T026 to T031 run `HOOK`, the advisor CLI or a store reader, and each is a coordinator task.\n233: - [ ] CHK-032 [P1] The default record file stays private. Evidence: `V tests/metrics-file-permissions.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed in T012.\n234: <!-- /ANCHOR:security -->\n235: \n236: ---\n237: \n238: <!-- ANCHOR:docs -->\n239: ## Documentation\n240: \n241: - [ ] CHK-040 [P1] `spec.md`, `plan.md`, `tasks.md` and `implementation-summary.md` state the same numbers. Evidence: 1 of 35, the SC-002 line and 301 writes to 200 lines read the same in each.\n242: - [ ] CHK-041 [P1] The five documents and the advisor leg match the code (T007 to T011, T017, T025). Evidence: their verify commands print what they say.\n243: <!-- /ANCHOR:docs -->\n244: \n245: ---\n246: \n247: <!-- ANCHOR:file-org -->\n248: ## File Organization\n249: \n250: - [ ] CHK-050 [P1] Every measurement lives in `scratch/` and no probe script is left in the tree. Evidence: `ls scratch` lists the files the tasks name.\n251: - [ ] CHK-051 [P1] No file outside the tasks' list changed (T033). Evidence: the T033 status line.\n252: <!-- /ANCHOR:file-org -->\n253: \n254: ---\n255: \n256: <!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n257: ## Verification Summary\n258: \n259: | Category | Total | Verified |\n260: |----------|-------|----------|\n261: | P0 Items | 14 | 0/14 |\n262: | P1 Items | 13 | 0/13 |\n263: | P2 Items | 0 | 0/0 |\n264: \n265: **Verification Date**: 2026-11-13\n266: <!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/015-health-default-and-brief-refinements/tasks.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794566779650,"end":1794566780127}}}}
